# ── Chapter 17 fidelity pins: "How Public Power Is Built" ──────────────────
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. Run:
#   ./verify.sh --only book-1/17-how-public-power-is-built.pins.nibli
#   ./verify.sh          # the real check — the line above cannot see
#                        # the cross-file reconciliation or the prose guards
#
# The chapter's case lists tests/pins/records/child_with_nobody/fixture.nibli.
#
# The tiers, the bodies, the deadlock routes, the secession route and the
# result contract all conclude `authority(body, power, record)` from a complete
# state-form record, and those records are written inside the family's own
# cases rather than duplicated here:
#   tests/pins/state-form/main-01 .. main-64   the powers this chapter names,
#                                       one complete record each: enumerated
#                                       common competence and regional residual
#                                       authority, subsidiarity displacement and
#                                       interim allocation, Assembly lawmaking,
#                                       revenue, spending, oversight and
#                                       amendment initiation, Regions Council
#                                       selection, reasoned return and
#                                       federal-settlement consent, executive
#                                       execution, confidence and constructive
#                                       replacement, the President's selection,
#                                       appointment, promulgation and
#                                       continuity, ordinary-court relief,
#                                       general invalidation, procedure review,
#                                       the alternate panel, the appointments
#                                       function, cause-only removal and the
#                                       vacancy fallback
#   tests/pins/state-form/counterfactual-01 .. counterfactual-17   what stops
#                                       deriving when a required condition is
#                                       taken out of the source
#   tests/pins/integrity/               the money, disclosure, districting,
#                                       opposition and coordination findings
# Every one of those is a legal effect over a supplied record. None of them
# staffs a body, holds an election, or establishes that an institution acted.
#
# The vocabulary probes below use one bare lexicon record with no authorised
# attesters, so they complete nothing; what they exercise is the closed list
# each name belongs to. The state-form block declares no single-valued scope
# and no record-ambiguity rule, so one record carries them all.
#
# WHAT FALSE MEANS HERE: a FALSE is pinned only where the KB could have said
# TRUE, and the comment says what would flip it.

:expect-pins 43

# ── "one current government, chamber, party coalition, profession or
# appointing source" — the closed list of sources the anti-capture rule names.
observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, CurrentGovernmentAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindScope).
? member(CurrentGovernmentAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, ChamberAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindScope).
? member(ChamberAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, PartyCoalitionAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindScope).
? member(PartyCoalitionAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, ProfessionAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindScope).
? member(ProfessionAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, SingleAppointingBodyAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindScope).
? member(SingleAppointingBodyAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

# "both direct and de facto appointment control observable" — the second is
# the one a divided-sources arrangement hides.
observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, DirectAppointmentControl, AppointmentControlModeScope).
? member(DirectAppointmentControl, AppointmentControlModeVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, DeFactoAppointmentControl, AppointmentControlModeScope).
? member(DeFactoAppointmentControl, AppointmentControlModeVocabulary).
# => TRUE

# ── "An office's own, household or controlled-entity interests" ───────────
observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, OwnMaterialInterest, MaterialInterestKindScope).
? member(OwnMaterialInterest, MaterialInterestKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, HouseholdMaterialInterest, MaterialInterestKindScope).
? member(HouseholdMaterialInterest, MaterialInterestKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, ControlledEntityMaterialInterest, MaterialInterestKindScope).
? member(ControlledEntityMaterialInterest, MaterialInterestKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

# "Gifts from counterparties and dealings through former holders face
# relationship-bound limits" — the relationships, by name.
observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, RegulatedCounterparty, CounterpartyRelationshipKindScope).
? member(RegulatedCounterparty, CounterpartyRelationshipKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, ContractingCounterparty, CounterpartyRelationshipKindScope).
? member(ContractingCounterparty, CounterpartyRelationshipKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, AdjudicatedCounterparty, CounterpartyRelationshipKindScope).
? member(AdjudicatedCounterparty, CounterpartyRelationshipKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, AppointedCounterparty, CounterpartyRelationshipKindScope).
? member(AppointedCounterparty, CounterpartyRelationshipKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

# The three shapes an office-integrity finding can take.
observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, ConflictedAct, OfficeIntegrityModeScope).
? member(ConflictedAct, OfficeIntegrityModeVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, CounterpartyBenefit, OfficeIntegrityModeScope).
? member(CounterpartyBenefit, OfficeIntegrityModeVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, FormerHolderCounterpartyDealing, OfficeIntegrityModeScope).
? member(FormerHolderCounterpartyDealing, OfficeIntegrityModeVocabulary).
# => TRUE

# ── "the kinds of payer, instrument and recipient" ────────────────────────
# "Enterprise treasuries, unions and voluntary civic associations remain
# different kinds; relabelling cannot replace examination of who controls
# the payment."
observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, PersonPayer, PoliticalFinancePayerKindScope).
? member(PersonPayer, PoliticalFinancePayerKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, EnterpriseTreasuryPayer, PoliticalFinancePayerKindScope).
? member(EnterpriseTreasuryPayer, PoliticalFinancePayerKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, UnionPayer, PoliticalFinancePayerKindScope).
? member(UnionPayer, PoliticalFinancePayerKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, VoluntaryCivicAssociationPayer, PoliticalFinancePayerKindScope).
? member(VoluntaryCivicAssociationPayer, PoliticalFinancePayerKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, OutsideJurisdictionPayer, PoliticalFinancePayerKindScope).
? member(OutsideJurisdictionPayer, PoliticalFinancePayerKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, ControllingPartyPayer, PoliticalFinancePayerKindScope).
? member(ControllingPartyPayer, PoliticalFinancePayerKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

# The instruments, so a loan or an in-kind provision cannot be filed as
# something the record does not examine.
observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, ContributionInstrument, PoliticalFinanceInstrumentKindScope).
? member(ContributionInstrument, PoliticalFinanceInstrumentKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, ExpenditureInstrument, PoliticalFinanceInstrumentKindScope).
? member(ExpenditureInstrument, PoliticalFinanceInstrumentKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, InKindProvisionInstrument, PoliticalFinanceInstrumentKindScope).
? member(InKindProvisionInstrument, PoliticalFinanceInstrumentKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, LoanOrGuaranteeInstrument, PoliticalFinanceInstrumentKindScope).
? member(LoanOrGuaranteeInstrument, PoliticalFinanceInstrumentKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, PurchasedIndependentAdvocacyInstrument, PoliticalFinanceInstrumentKindScope).
? member(PurchasedIndependentAdvocacyInstrument, PoliticalFinanceInstrumentKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

# And the recipients.
observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, CandidateRecipient, PoliticalFinanceRecipientKindScope).
? member(CandidateRecipient, PoliticalFinanceRecipientKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, PartyOrCoalitionRecipient, PoliticalFinanceRecipientKindScope).
? member(PartyOrCoalitionRecipient, PoliticalFinanceRecipientKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, BallotQuestionRecipient, PoliticalFinanceRecipientKindScope).
? member(BallotQuestionRecipient, PoliticalFinanceRecipientKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, OfficeHolderRecipient, PoliticalFinanceRecipientKindScope).
? member(OfficeHolderRecipient, PoliticalFinanceRecipientKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, PublicDecisionRecipient, PoliticalFinanceRecipientKindScope).
? member(PublicDecisionRecipient, PoliticalFinanceRecipientKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE

# ── "A district plan may not be drawn to entrench a party, coalition or
# incumbent, or to dilute a protected ground." ────────────────────────────
observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, PartyOrCoalitionEntrenchment, ForbiddenDistrictingPurposeScope).
? member(PartyOrCoalitionEntrenchment, ForbiddenDistrictingPurposeVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, IncumbentEntrenchment, ForbiddenDistrictingPurposeScope).
? member(IncumbentEntrenchment, ForbiddenDistrictingPurposeVocabulary).
# => TRUE

observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, ProtectedGroundDilution, ForbiddenDistrictingPurposeScope).
? member(ProtectedGroundDilution, ForbiddenDistrictingPurposeVocabulary).
# => TRUE
# The lists are closed, which is what makes writing them out worth anything: a
# kind nobody enacted is in none of them, however it is spelled.
observe(PowerLexiconWriter, PowerLexiconRecord, UnapprovedAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindScope).
? member(UnapprovedAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindVocabulary).
# => FALSE

# ── The child with nobody ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "Nothing in this chapter reads a person at all." The whole apparatus above is
# in the record and the child's own conclusions are exactly what they were.
? person(Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Expresses, Nell).
# => TRUE

# "The ballot is not on the floor" — said plainly here rather than blurred.
? decide(Nell, Ballot).
# => FALSE

? false(Nell).
# => FALSE

? prisoner(Nell).
# => FALSE

# A person is not a body. Writing a complete state-form record that named this
# child as the holder is what would flip this, and nobody has written one.
? authority(Nell, FSPOW_005, PowerLexiconRecord).
# => FALSE
